          "turn_index": 1,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Is there a questionnaire they use for it?",
          "answer": "Yes. The guidance on anxiety screening (guideline-anxiety-screening-and-first-line-care) says the instrument most often used is a seven-item generalized anxiety disorder questionnaire. It is used both to screen for the problem and to track how severe it is. Scores are grouped into bands: 5 is mild, 10 is moderate and 15 is severe. A score of 10 is the point where further assessment usually follows.\n\nThe questionnaire is only a screening tool. It cannot confirm a condition by itself, so a clinician would still need to look at your full situation. Bringing up the questionnaire with a doctor or mental health professional is a reasonable step. You can ask whether they use it and what your result would mean.\n\nThe search results did not include the questions themselves or say how to score them at home, so I can't walk you through the test here. Some other results in the search were about unrelated conditions, so I have not used them.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
